            <ArticleTitle>Giant simple hepatic cyst: a case report and review of relevant literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>293-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4314/ahs.v15i1.40</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Giant cysts of the liver are uncommon. Symptoms are related primarily to the mass effect of the enlarging cyst.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To highlight the challenges of management of giant simple hepatic cyst in a resource limited setting.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE REPORT" NlmCategory="METHODS">Presented is a 58-year-old seamstress with a 5-year history of an enlarging abdominal mass with easy satiety. Surgery revealed an exophytic giant simple hepatic cyst arising from liver segment IV that drained 4.6 litres of serous fluid.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Simple hepatic cyst can attain giant dimensions and should be considered in the differential diagnosis of intraabdominal masses.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
